{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"additional_concerns\":[\"The classification rule combines an automatic 50%-of-NAV route with a discretionary SFC designation route; missing exposure measurement or designation records leave the executable result unknown.\",\"The circular references separate authorities for complex-product sale requirements, UT Code section 7.3, and the LAF circular, but those authorities are not supplied and should not be inferred from the circular alone.\",\"The representation includes a below-50% condition for discretionary designation; the circular footnote supports that context, but the operative designation decision for a particular Fund remains unestablished. \"],\"checks\":[{\"authority\":{\"dependency_ids\":[],\"rationale\":\"The claim is supported by the retained circular itself; no additional external dependency is required to establish that the SFC may designate a covered Fund case by case.\",\"status\":\"NONE_DECLARED\"},\"candidate_id\":\"node.65050459a1ce3ffe5cff6887\",\"claim_id\":\"claim.6583b0dfd390304d78bedde0\",\"executable_correspondence\":{\"rationale\":\"The representation preserves the case-by-case permission, the holistic approach, the below-50% footnote context, and the LAF exclusion.\",\"representation_quotes\":[\"On a case-by-case basis, the SFC may also designate a Fund as a complex product, taking into account factors including, without limitation:\",\"In assessing whether the complex product designation is warranted7, the SFC will adopt a holistic approach taking into account the specific circumstances of the case.\",\"In cases where the Fund’s aggregate direct and indirect exposures to private market assets are less than 50% of the Fund’s NAV.\"],\"status\":\"PRESERVES\"},\"followup_questions\":[\"Is there an operative SFC designation decision for the assessed Fund at the assessment time?\"],\"question_relation\":{\"evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"On a case-by-case basis, the SFC